{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted","id":1122952,"title":"Shouldn't Kindred be Wyrm *and* Weaver tainted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-31T03:15:59-07:00","id":1122952,"title":"Shouldn't Kindred be Wyrm *and* Weaver tainted?","content":"So Vampires are stuck in the moment of their death. Absolute stasis; this is confirmed as of Time of Thin Blood. Vitae is a preservative, the best one in existence; it makes animals and humans live forever, and it keeps a Vampire stuck in a default state that they revert to each night.<br /> <br /> I can see the justification for Wyrm taint, certainly. They're a dead body walking around, feeding on living people in a parasitic way. BUT, considering that they can only exist because of stasis (a 'beautiful corpse' as V20 puts it, existing forever), shouldn't they reek of the Weaver too? If you look at the behaviour of your average Vampire, Weaver taint makes more and more sense; Kindred who reject stability don't last very long, and the possibility of living forever makes many cautious builders rather than rabid destroyers.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, I think that 'Vitae as a preservative' could be a good explanation for why Garou and Fera are so violently allergic to Kindred blood; they're living creatures who embody the best and worst aspects of being alive, and part of that is aging and eventually dying. Having Ghouldom be an easy out for age-anxious Shifters should be a terrible oversight on the part of Spirits, as it would be a fast-track to serving the Wyrm. Just look at the Garou's treatment of the Gurahl; many of them WANT an easy way out of mortality, they want to be eternal warriors and fight the good fight forever in many cases. Making them violently allergic to one of the most obvious methods of immortality is a smart move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T03:25:29-07:00","id":1122954,"title":"","content":"They do? just sense weaver/imbalance etc is alot rarer than &quot;Sense wyrm&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T03:35:37-07:00","id":1122956,"title":"","content":"I was like, &quot;Aren't they?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T05:12:19-07:00","id":1122975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1122956#post1122956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was like, &quot;Aren't they?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see, so it's just a matter of Garou having Sense Wyrm and not Sense Weaver?<br /> <br /> Okay, so moving on from that, why are Kindred &quot;creatures of the Wyrm&quot; rather than being seen as &quot;creatures linked to two members of the triat, like practically everything is&quot;? Saying Vampires are &quot;servants of the Wyrm&quot; feels like willful ignorance on the part of Garou at this point... or is it that they are MORE tainted by the Wyrm than the Weaver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T06:06:03-07:00","id":1122989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1122975#post1122975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I see, so it's just a matter of Garou having Sense Wyrm and not Sense Weaver?<br /> <br /> Okay, so moving on from that, why are Kindred &quot;creatures of the Wyrm&quot; rather than being seen as &quot;creatures linked to two members of the triat, like practically everything is&quot;? Saying Vampires are &quot;servants of the Wyrm&quot; feels like willful ignorance on the part of Garou at this point... or is it that they are MORE tainted by the Wyrm than the Weaver?</div> </div> </div> </div>The conceit that Garou have the &quot;Super inner workings of reality worked out&quot; is not one that's backed up by W:TA. They have a focus on the Wyrm as their enemy. There's no &quot;Defend Gaia from all forms of Imbalance&quot; Litany passage. There is &quot;Combat the Wyrm wherever it dwells&quot;. There is a strong undercurrent that perhaps in GENERALLY ignoring the Growth of the Weaver while focusing on the wyrm that has been one of the many reasons the world is dying.<br /> <br /> But really your average Kindred could be 30 parts weaver to 10 parts wyrm those 30 parts weaver are something not even your most weaverphiliac Glasswalker is going to give a single damn about. And the myth they tell about the first Kindred as much incorporates the weaver as the wyrm.<br /> <br /> IF one wants to get crossover friendly one could argue that kindred who are the most &quot;Weavery&quot; tend to be ones with particularly High Paths thus their aura covering up their &quot;natural&quot; triat balance, so another reason why the weaver connection isn't played up much, but this is pure conjecture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T06:39:22-07:00","id":1122998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1122989#post1122989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The conceit that Garou have the &quot;Super inner workings of reality worked out&quot; is not one that's backed up by W:TA. They have a focus on the Wyrm as their enemy. There's no &quot;Defend Gaia from all forms of Imbalance&quot; Litany passage. There is &quot;Combat the Wyrm wherever it dwells&quot;. There is a strong undercurrent that perhaps in GENERALLY ignoring the Growth of the Weaver while focusing on the wyrm that has been one of the many reasons the world is dying.<br /> <br /> But really your average Kindred could be 30 parts weaver to 10 parts wyrm those 30 parts weaver are something not even your most weaverphiliac Glasswalker is going to give a single damn about. And the myth they tell about the first Kindred as much incorporates the weaver as the wyrm.<br /> <br /> IF one wants to get crossover friendly one could argue that kindred who are the most &quot;Weavery&quot; tend to be ones with particularly High Paths thus their aura covering up their &quot;natural&quot; triat balance, so another reason why the weaver connection isn't played up much, but this is pure conjecture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, really? Like not &quot;combat the Wyrm's imbalance and madness&quot;, but &quot;combat the Wyrm&quot;? So from a Garou perspective they should fight to stop ALL forms of Wyrm-influence? Eating meat? Fighting? Killing? Fire? Natural disasters? Disease? No wonder they wanted to Gurahl to let them become immortal zombie-Garou...<br /> <br /> Well it's Humanity 7 or Higher I believe, and I think that's just a matter of Vampires having a natural tendency to shield their true nature if they are high up a Path. Even Path of the Beast 10 *seems* super human at first glance as of DAV20 (my personal fave interpretation, which I argue supersedes V20 and all others); since they're a predator, the better the control they have over their beast (Humanity, or any Path), the less the mask slips. If their &quot;true nature&quot; has Wyrm Taint, then a high Path will hide that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 07-31-2017, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:09:17-07:00","id":1123007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1122998#post1122998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, really? Like not &quot;combat the Wyrm's imbalance and madness&quot;, but &quot;combat the Wyrm&quot;? So from a Garou perspective they should fight to stop ALL forms of Wyrm-influence? Eating meat? Fighting? Killing? Fire? Natural disasters? Disease? No wonder they wanted to Gurahl to let them become immortal zombie-Garou...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is &quot;of the wyrm&quot; has levels of interpretation, and you have different ways of fighting. With say the COG being more prone to trying to clean/redeem vs other tribes. There's also obviously a limited number of Garou so they have focus on what they consider the best use of their limited resourses(another reason why they don't pay much attention to the weaver!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well it's Humanity 7 or Higher I believe, and I think that's just a matter of Vampires having a natural tendency to shield their true nature if they are high up a Path. Even Path of the Beast 10 *seems* super human at first glance as of DAV20 (my personal fave interpretation, which I argue supersedes V20 and all others); since they're a predator, the better the control they have over their beast (Humanity, or any Path), the less the mask slips. If their &quot;true nature&quot; has Wyrm Taint, then a high Path will hide that. </div> </div> </div>Well Vampires have Bearing/aura depending on their Road/Path the Aura/bearing of Humanity is normality so people think you are normal and cover up discrepencies. I'd presume other paths would equally &quot;hide&quot; wyrm taint if it goes against wyrm taint.. I'd imagine say someone on Typhon is going to be quite wyrmy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:22:24-07:00","id":1123011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1122998#post1122998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, really? Like not &quot;combat the Wyrm's imbalance and madness&quot;, but &quot;combat the Wyrm&quot;? So from a Garou perspective they should fight to stop ALL forms of Wyrm-influence? Eating meat? Fighting? Killing? Fire? Natural disasters? Disease? No wonder they wanted to Gurahl to let them become immortal zombie-Garou...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, fundamentalist crusaders societies need simple tenets to sustains their ideology. Telling a young cub raised in the garou fuck up society &quot;one day we will destroy all the wyrm and save the world&quot; is a simple message to get across and get behind in that fervent &quot;lets-not-think-this-too-much&quot;, it paint the wyrm as the unquestioned enemy to be defeated and make it a &quot;quantifiable&quot; goal (that is, destroying all the wyrm) even if it isnt doable.<br /> <br /> Saying the more nuanced &quot;we will some day bring the wyrm back to balance because in reality the wyrm is still necessary and the fact that its minions killed your pack/friend/etc is just a tragic case of macro biology and you are just Gaia white cells fighting a liver infection. And even if we bring balance to the wyrm we will either be eradicated having fulfilled our purpose or we will continue this war forever as the eternal white cell dying to keep the planet alive whenever it unbalances itself with no end&quot;<br /> <br /> This leave the full of rage Garou with no enemy or simple black and white situation to face, and forces him to think of the bigger picture. Which might bring the Garou into a conclusion that the Nation wouldnt approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:41:17-07:00","id":1123016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1123007#post1123007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Vampires have Bearing/aura depending on their Road/Path the Aura/bearing of Humanity is normality so people think you are normal and cover up discrepencies. I'd presume other paths would equally &quot;hide&quot; wyrm taint if it goes against wyrm taint.. I'd imagine say someone on Typhon is going to be quite wyrmy...</div> </div> </div> </div>In V20 Humanity's bearing is Normalcy, but in DAV20 that's a default thing for all Paths (Roads/Paths/Humanity), being passably human, even the most inhuman paths. The Bearings are something additional in each case, like seeming dangerous or seeming devout etc.<br /> <br /> So the DAV20 answer (and my answer) to how wyrm-tainted someone seems on Path of Typhon, is &quot;well at 1-6 they're going to be HORRIBLY wyrm-tainted to a Garou's senses, but at 7+ they're going to be pass as something else under Sense Wyrm and they're going to stand up to a lot of superficial inspections of whether they're a Vampire or not&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 07-31-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:40:51-07:00","id":1123030,"title":"","content":"Vampires aren't in true stasis. Rather, their beasts feed on life to give them a pseudo-stasis. Essentially, they have in them Rage that heals them by converting the Gnosis of others into Rage. Their healing and immortality is therefore closer to the diff 8 Rage roll that Garou can make when on the verge of death: an ugly berzerk urge of the Wyrm to avoid death rather than Gaian healing or Weaver stasis. That's my head-canon, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 07-31-2017, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:54:20-07:00","id":1123033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1123030#post1123030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires aren't in true stasis. Rather, their beasts feed on life to give them a pseudo-stasus. Essentially, they have in them Rage that heals them by converting the Gnosis of others into Rage. Their healing and immortality is therefore closer to the diff 8 Rage roll that Garou can make when on the verge of death: an ugly berzerk urge of the Wyrm to avoid death rather than Gaian healing or Weaver stasus. That's my head-canon, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very nice way of putting it in WTA terms... if I were running a WTA-centric universe I'd definitely frame it that way :-)<br /> <br /> However I think that's a lovely way for Werewolves to think about Vampiric healing, like the rage of the Wyrm clawing to stay &quot;alive&quot;, in a grim parody of what once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:04:43-07:00","id":1123037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1122975#post1122975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I see, so it's just a matter of Garou having Sense Wyrm and not Sense Weaver?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have Sense Weaver too, it's just less common.<br /> But remember: the Weaver is still an enemy for the Garou, just not as important as the other one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, so moving on from that, why are Kindred &quot;creatures of the Wyrm&quot; rather than being seen as &quot;creatures linked to two members of the triat, like practically everything is&quot;? Saying Vampires are &quot;servants of the Wyrm&quot; feels like willful ignorance on the part of Garou at this point... or is it that they are MORE tainted by the Wyrm than the Weaver? </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm-taint is caused by the Curse of Caine: they're dead yet still living, their mere existence is breaking the laws of nature. Of course they're kinda different from willing servants of the Wyrm, but most werewolves do not make any difference since the Jihad nurtures the right conditions for the Wyrm to prosper. And the fact that the maejin-incarnas ruling over Malfeas are 13, just like the number of Antediluvians, really does them no favour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So from a Garou perspective they should fight to stop ALL forms of Wyrm-influence? Eating meat? Fighting? Killing? Fire? Natural disasters? Disease? No wonder they wanted to Gurahl to let them become immortal zombie-Garou </div> </div> </div>The point is not fighting entropy as a concept. Entropy is part of Gaia's world, and there still are uncorrupted entropy spirits around that did not follow the Wyrm in its madness. The Wyrm is an aspect of entropy, that took its own form as a spirit strong enough to outclass even Celestines and that grows stronger with the corruption of Earth and the creatures living there.<br /> The Garou are not battling the idea that all things must eventually ends, just the entity trying to destroy everything without leaving room for a new birth (and its servants). And yes, some will be fanatics, some will be ignorant and some others more open-minded, and sometimes the open-mindness will bring more harm than good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:57:33-07:00","id":1123080,"title":"","content":"Okay this seems increasingly garbled... is the Wyrm the Spiritual Incarnation of entropy, destruction and &quot;undoing&quot; in WTA or not? I swear the whole point of the Triat is that they are on a scale that goes beyond all but a few spirits (Gaia, Helios, Luna etc.)?<br /> <br /> I understand that there are subordinate spirits to each of the Triat (and Gaia) but it seems weird that you can fight the Wyrm without fighting Entropy as a concept.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fighting the Wyrm's madness&quot; or &quot;fighting the Wyrm where it shows its madness&quot; would make a lot more sense than fighting the Wyrm, and as far as I can see that's what the Garou are doing. &quot;Fighting the Wyrm&quot; feels like a serious over-simplification...<br /> <br /> But history DOES tell us that the Garou are kind of dumb on this issue. One unverified source tells them that The Wyrm lives inside of an amber prison, and they charge in and attack it en masse. Do... do they really think they can destroy destruction as a concept? It feels like this is too dumb even for historical NPCs... or maybe that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T13:11:14-07:00","id":1123140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1123080#post1123080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay this seems increasingly garbled... is the Wyrm the Spiritual Incarnation of entropy, destruction and &quot;undoing&quot; in WTA or not? I swear the whole point of the Triat is that they are on a scale that goes beyond all but a few spirits (Gaia, Helios, Luna etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond Luna and Helios, but by default, not Gaia, since Gaia encompasses everything. The members of the Trait been referred to as Supernals in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand that there are subordinate spirits to each of the Triat (and Gaia) but it seems weird that you can fight the Wyrm without fighting Entropy as a concept. </div> </div> </div>You are, but not the way you're thinking. Recall that in Werewolf, if you kill the spirit of something, it crumbles and falls to ruin. It's working off of an animistic reality, so whatever has a spirit is more real than what doesn't..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Fighting the Wyrm's madness&quot; or &quot;fighting the Wyrm where it shows its madness&quot; would make a lot more sense than fighting the Wyrm, and as far as I can see that's what the Garou are doing. &quot;Fighting the Wyrm&quot; feels like a serious over-simplification... </div> </div> </div>Calling it the Wyrm is, as well. You need to focus on certain key points in order to utilize force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But history DOES tell us that the Garou are kind of dumb on this issue. One unverified source tells them that The Wyrm lives inside of an amber prison, and they charge in and attack it en masse. Do... do they really think they can destroy destruction as a concept? It feels like this is too dumb even for historical NPCs... or maybe that's just me. </div> </div> </div>History in Revised and W20 told us that Garou were getting wise to no one in the Triat actually being their friend, and the need for them to re-evaluate their target priorities and methods of operation. The major leaders in NA and Europe, King Albrecht and Margrave Konietzko, had a background effect of promoting diversification of the Garou Nation's efforts as a whole when they held influence.<br /> <br /> Before that, they were mostly concerned with fighting horrid gribbly monsters most of the time, because that got you readily-recognized Renown (and, thus, Rank). They didn't really deal with much that was larger than an Incarna, and that was typically by tearing out the supports that would have allowed it a ticket to more influence in the Gaia Realm. Think Call of Chtulhu, but with substantially more resilient and combat-capable investigators that don't have to worry nearly so much about SAN loss, and also, it's possible for you to kill a wide scale of the horrid monsters that cultists summon forth. Once you get to, say, Zmei and large Thunderwyrms, though, you start to have problems, and you might need to consider that it's better to just scour out the cults before they do something, so that you can deal with more problems, even if it means you won't have esteem that might bring you other, more direct capabilities courtesy of your spirit allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:38:06-07:00","id":1123665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1122952-shouldn-t-kindred-be-wyrm-and-weaver-tainted?p=1123080#post1123080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay this seems increasingly garbled... is the Wyrm the Spiritual Incarnation of entropy, destruction and &quot;undoing&quot; in WTA or not? I swear the whole point of the Triat is that they are on a scale that goes beyond all but a few spirits (Gaia, Helios, Luna etc.)?<br /> <br /> I understand that there are subordinate spirits to each of the Triat (and Gaia) but it seems weird that you can fight the Wyrm without fighting Entropy as a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are fighting entropy, but only a part of the entropy.<br /> Like, in the Apocalypse setting (the manual that closed the previous edition of Werewolf) Gaia could have been both in Pangea and in the Summer Country. How? Because both realms expressed two different aspects of Gaia, the primordial life and the nurturing mother. Or then again, the Lion spirit (former White Howlers' totem) now is into the Griffin's brood, but the supplements already described a second Lion incarna, specifying that it was not the same Lion-spirit.<br /> <br /> In the Umbra, Spirits are concepts that took life on their own, but the same concept can give birth to multiple spirits. So yes, killing the Wyrm would &quot;kill&quot; entropy, but not in the sense that the world would get static and deathless. Of course, assuming that I'm not horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do... do they really think they can destroy destruction as a concept? </div> </div> </div>In Apocalypse was also said that killing the avatar of Gaia would have not destroyed the Earth nor the life on it, but it would have left it without the ability to evolve and renew. So yes, killing the Wyrm could probably manage to destroy a fair share of the concept of destruction, and perhaps leave the place to re-form another, better &quot;destruction&quot;, much alike as how Dream is reborn in Sandman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 08-01-2017, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:42:47-07:00","id":1123666,"title":"","content":"[this was a double posting. sorry and please delete]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:41:10-07:00","id":1125042,"title":"","content":"I think the confusion is rooted in White Wolf's mixed use of the idea of spiritual decay. Much of White Wolf's lore implicitly accepts the idea that there is a natural order, and that anything outside the natural order has spiritually rotted. I.e. there is natural and unnatural and unnatural is evil. The thing is, though, that this idea is antithetical to the modern mind, and breaks down under rigorous analysis like most religious ideas. For example, is a machine unnatural? Humans naturally evolved the brain that made the machine. It is as much an extension of us as claws. What about nuclear waste? Same deal as machines.<br /> <br /> White Wolf's books deal with this issue rather randomly. Some things treat natural as good and unnatural as evil. Some deal with the complexity of the issue from a scientific perspective. Some things lurch into an implicitly Judaeo-christian perspective even if religion is never mentioned. It's all rather random, with the only unifying thread being what a writer thought would either make a good story-hook, or be balanced mechanically for a game. I say random, but it might be more accurate to say that much of it is rooted in the writers subconscious, in whether his mindset is more heavily influenced by Western culture, science, or his putting himself in the werewolves place and writing as though their religious mindset is correct.<br /> <br /> So the books end up being, on a certain level, a set of self-portraits rather than a consistent example of world-building.<br /> <br /> So, is the Wyrm entropy? Depending on what book and what chapter you read, the Wyrm can be Entropy, or it can be Evil-Incarnate from the perspective of nature-worshipers who view everything unnatural as spiritually decayed, or it can be Evil-Incarnate from the very different perspective of Western culture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T19:45:39-07:00","id":1125058,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'd say that the point is not really thinking about &quot;natural&quot;, but about &quot;harmony&quot;, the ability to survive in an environment by taking its resources without depleting them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, is the Wyrm entropy? Depending on what book and what chapter you read, the Wyrm can be Entropy, or it can be Evil-Incarnate from the perspective of nature-worshipers who view everything unnatural as spiritually decayed, or it can be Evil-Incarnate from the very different perspective of Western culture. </div> </div> </div>I usually solve the dilemma through a MtA perspective: Chakravanti are not Nephandi, and Entropy is not the Wyrm. Even if the Wyrm is Entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:30:46-07:00","id":1125073,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm is a primal force of destruction, but not necessarily evil or the enemy of Gaia. Garou lore looks back to the &quot;Wyrm of Balance&quot; in primeval prehistory, where his role as a member of the Triat was to maintain balance between the creative Wyld and the ordering-preserving Weaver. When the Wyrm was attacked by the Weaver, and trapped in her webs, he went insane. That's when the Wyrm's destructive power turned into a corrupting, evil force, and made him an enemy to Gaia. Ideally, it would be nice if the Garou could work on purifying the Wyrm and restoring his sanity, but that's a task that even the most powerful of Incarnae have been unable to achieve, so it's way beyond the Garou to try. What they can do is fight the Wyrm's activity in the realms they live in, purifying what they can, and keeping the growing corruption at bay. Anything more sophisticated than &quot;Fight the Wyrm&quot; is above and beyond the werewolves' abilities, so that's what they preach.<br /> <br /> To the original question, sure, it's reasonable to suggest that vampires are more Weaver-creatures than Wyrm-creatures, but I don't think the Garou would describe the smell of the Weaver as &quot;taint.&quot; You might be able to detect weaver-association with a &quot;name the spirit&quot; gift, but if you did, that wouldn't call out the subject as an enemy. Wyrm-taint, on the other hand, is all the justification a werewolf needs to consider someone an enemy, or at the very least, someone in dire need of spiritual cleansing, which isn't a treatment that works on leeches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}